## Session Workflow (Required for Every Agent)

### Start of every session
1. Read `AGENTS.md` — your role, start conditions, and handoff chain
2. Read `SOUL.md` — operating principles
3. Read `active-project.md` — which project is active
4. **Read `projects/[active-project]/HANDOFF.md`** — check for rows where **To = your role** and **Status = ⏳ Pending**. If one exists, that is your assignment. Start there, not at the TODO.
5. Read `projects/[active-project]/AGENT-TODO.md` — current priority queue
6. Read `projects/[active-project]/AGENT-SESSION-LOG.md` — recent history
7. Begin work at the top of the Priority Queue unless a HANDOFF.md assignment takes priority

### On every commit / completed task
Update all three tracking files in the same action:
- Check off completed items in `AGENT-TODO.md`
- Add a session log row in `AGENT-SESSION-LOG.md`
- Update `AGENT-TODO.md` with any new items discovered during work

### End of every session
Do a final pass on both files:
- Ensure all completed items are checked off in `AGENT-TODO.md`
- Ensure the session log row accurately reflects what was done
- Move completed items to the Completed table in `AGENT-TODO.md`

