## Active Project Path — How to Find It

**Every session, determine the absolute project path before writing any files.**

```bash
# Step 1: Read active-project.md — it contains the relative path
# e.g. "Project Path: projects/AIRR"

# Step 2: Full absolute path is:
~/.openclaw/workspace/projects/[project-name]/
```

**All files go inside the project directory.** Never write to the workspace root or a workspace-level folder:
- ✅ `~/.openclaw/workspace/projects/MYAPP/assets/logos/logo.svg`
- ❌ `~/.openclaw/workspace/assets/myapp/logo.svg`   ← WRONG
- ✅ `~/.openclaw/workspace/projects/MYAPP/tickets/open/TASK-001.md`
- ❌ `~/.openclaw/workspace/tickets/open/TASK-001.md`   ← WRONG

