## GitHub Workflow (Required for GitHub-Backed Projects)

**Check if the project has a GitHub remote:**
```bash
cat ~/.openclaw/workspace/projects/[name]/.project-meta.json
# Look for "remote_url" — if present, this project is GitHub-backed
```

**After completing ANY deliverable** (code, assets, docs, tickets), commit and push:
```bash
PROJECT=~/.openclaw/workspace/projects/[name]
git -C $PROJECT add -A
git -C $PROJECT commit -m "Brief description of what was done [Agent: your-role]"
git -C $PROJECT push
```

Do this at the end of every session. **The operator and other agents rely on GitHub as the shared source of truth.** Files that exist only locally are invisible to everyone else.

### Standard folder structure inside a GitHub-backed project
```
[project-root]/
  assets/
    logos/        ← brand logos and wordmarks (.svg, .png)
    banners/      ← hero images, headers (.jpg, .svg)
    icons/        ← app icons, favicons (.png)
    graphics/     ← UI illustrations, state graphics (.png)
    mockups/      ← UI mockup screenshots (.png)
  tickets/
    open/         ← active MC tickets (BUG-NNN.md, FEAT-NNN.md, etc.)
    closed/       ← resolved tickets
  docs/           ← design docs, specs, research
  src/ or app/    ← source code (varies by project)
```

